The built window goes here. `make ui` writes it, and CI writes it before it
builds or releases anything.

This file lives in ui/public, which vite copies into dist on every build, and
a copy of it is committed at ui/dist/.keep as well. The committed one is what
go:embed finds on a clone that has never run a build; the copied one is what
puts it back after vite empties dist. Neither alone is enough: without the
first `go build ./...` fails on a fresh clone, and without the second the
release refuses to publish from a tree git calls dirty.
